
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- 8. causal context-fiber record compression
-- Zero search, zero hardcoded delimiters or modalities, zero probability, zero stored tables.
-- Directly composes the repository's own architecture:
--   * Well-founded order & earliest content (docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub §§1-4, 7):
--     at point t, the earlier record R_{<t} uniquely determines the context fiber Sel(t) = Fib_c(c_t)
--     at every depth k = 4, 3, 2, 1, 0 without search.
--   * Contractible vs. non-contractible continuation fibers (lib/fiber.cub, lib/observation.cub):
--     when the transported continuations agree, encoding approaches 0 bits; when an innovation occurs,
--     exact fiber relaxation (warrants-refine) excludes ruled-out continuations and steps to depth k-1,
--     down to earliest-content ground coding over the remaining unseen alphabet.
--   * Equivalence quotienting (index-upto, lib/repeats.cub): parameterized by any q : Word → Word,
--     so identifying symbols fuses contexts and shrinks continuation fibers automatically.
--   * Exact discrete rANS (Section 7): LIFO encoding folds right-to-left while the causal state
--     advances left-to-right, so the decoder reconstructs the exact same fibers online from R_{<t}
--     with only a 2-to-3-byte framing header (zero vocabularies, zero frequency tables).

